        "heading": "Learn composition by studying how formulas are built.",
        "text": "<p>Reading a formula is one of the fastest ways to understand composition. The library gives you a large collection of educational formula studies to examine: which materials sit at the heart of a structure, which play supporting roles, and how small proportions of a powerful material can change the whole.</p><p>Studied alongside the lessons — and, where you have the materials, rebuilt at the bench — they show how theory becomes a finished fragrance.</p>",
